            <ArticleTitle>Soft on sticks: an evidence-based practice approach to reduce children's needlestick pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>208-15</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NCQ.0b013e31820e11de</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Soft on Sticks is a comprehensive, interdisciplinary, evidence-based practice initiative that was implemented to ensure consistent use of pharmacologic and nonpharmacologic interventions to reduce pain associated with needlestick procedures performed on children. Pre- and postimplementation data from children, parents, and nurses showed positive results from the practice change and identified areas for further improvement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
